<!--
    APIM operation policy for each of the three OTLP ingestion operations.

    PLACEHOLDER CONVENTION: this file uses __AI_NAME__ rather than the <AI_NAME>
    used elsewhere in this plugin. A '<' character is not legal inside an XML
    attribute value, so the angle-bracket form would make the file fail to parse
    before APIM ever saw it. Replace __AI_NAME__ with the Application Insights
    component name receiving client telemetry.

    Apply to all three operations, changing ONLY the backend-id:

        otlp-traces   =>  __AI_NAME__-otlp-ingestion-traces
        otlp-metrics  =>  __AI_NAME__-otlp-ingestion-metrics
        otlp-logs     =>  __AI_NAME__-otlp-ingestion-logs

    The body is OTLP protobuf and is passed through untouched. Do NOT add
    set-body, any policy that reads context.Request.Body, or a logger that
    captures the payload. Buffering a protobuf stream corrupts the upload, and
    the resulting ingestion failure is reported only as missing data.

    Compression: unlike the LLM API, there is no reason to strip Accept-Encoding
    here. Nothing downstream parses the response body for token counts.

    AUTHENTICATION. This template assumes the API requires an APIM subscription
    key, which APIM validates before this policy runs. To use Entra tokens
    instead (recommended, as no shared secret then reaches developer machines),
    set the API's subscriptionRequired to false and uncomment the
    validate-azure-ad-token block, which mirrors the LLM API. Clients then supply
    the token through the otelHeadersHelper setting rather than a static header.
-->
<policies>
    <inbound>
        <base />

        <!--
        <validate-azure-ad-token tenant-id="{{tenant-id}}" output-token-variable-name="jwt">
            <audiences>
                <audience>{{llm-api-audience}}</audience>
            </audiences>
        </validate-azure-ad-token>
        -->

        <set-backend-service id="apim-generated-otlp-backend" backend-id="__AI_NAME__-otlp-ingestion-traces" />
    </inbound>
    <backend>
        <base />
    </backend>
    <outbound>
        <base />
    </outbound>
    <on-error>
        <base />
    </on-error>
</policies>
